 {"id":"fabro-b065","title":"Blank stale seed context keys when routing Tracker empty","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:54:20.701Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:54:20.701Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md, extend the 'Tracker empty' JSON contract to also blank current_seed_id/title/brief and implementation_summary (it already clears review_verdict). In run 01M0T9B7T6XNM1D7JNY35Y6H8K the final planner pass closed seed fabro-8208, routed 'Tracker empty', yet its prompt still carried the dead seed's brief (1.6 KB) and implementation_summary (1.7 KB) as blob refs after budget demotion. Expected effect: the closing planner pass stops hauling stale seed context — fewer blob round-trips, smaller preambles, lower risk of the evidence-starvation pathology noted in the graph comments. Not a duplicate of fabro-b382, which covers prose duplication and sd call rules, not the context_updates key contract.","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-d936","title":"Make seeds-cli exit non-zero on errors (exit 0 masks failed tracker writes)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:54:20.848Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:54:20.848Z","description":"@os-eco/seeds-cli v0.5.15 prints errors like 'error: unknown option --format' to stdout with exit_code 0 — observed at events seq 62-63 of run 01M0T9B7T6XNM1D7JNY35Y6H8K when planner@1 ran sd update with --format json; only the model's text inspection caught the failed write. Change: seeds-cli exits non-zero and prints errors to stderr. Expected effect: removes a silent-corruption path for tracker writes (any exit-code-checking consumer or gate currently reads failure as success) and eliminates the observed wasted retry. Prompt-side syntax pinning is already covered by fabro-1399; this is the orthogonal CLI-side fix.","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-37a6","title":"Steer implementer to mechanical shell bulk edits for repetitive rewrites","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T23:01:45.209Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T23:01:45.209Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md, add one paragraph: for repetitive, pattern-shaped changes (call-site adaptation, renames), do one mechanical pass via shell (sd/perl -pi -e, already pinned in the runner image) and verify with one focused test, instead of N hand edits. Evidence: implementer@2 (fabro-28e8) was 42% of run cost ($0.486, 278s, 51.8k tokens) rewriting ~24 identical call sites one edit_file at a time, with 19 concurrent-write serialization warnings across passes and one swallowed-loop-body near-miss. Expected effect: refactor-class pass drops from ~$0.49/280s toward ~$0.12/112s; run cost -20-25%; eliminates the swallow-adjacent-code near-miss class. Distinct from fabro-4601 (sequential-edit discipline, different mechanism).","labels":["revision"]}
