+{"id":"fabro-797d","title":"Remove the gate acceptance bullet from the planner brief template","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T23:07:39.067Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T23:07:39.067Z","description":"In `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md`, delete the trailing \"Gate: `just qualitygate` green\" bullet from the brief format (it is the tester node's invariant, not the implementer's criterion), and in `prompts/implementer.md` step 4 make the rule absolute: never run `just qualitygate`; a smoke check is `go build` or one `go test -run`. In run 01M0TKB7H7DCWCR8TZY6SZPXD2 the implementer ran the full gate because the planner's brief bullet read as an acceptance criterion. Expected effect: no gate double-run per seed; value grows with gate duration. Root-cause fix upstream of open fabro-a67f's smoke whitelist.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-ffea","title":"Filter seed_cycles context to the four cycle keys","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T23:07:39.103Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T23:07:39.103Z","description":"Wherever the per-seed cycle counter is emitted or consumed (engine context key from closed fabro-45d0, or the guard-object contract in `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md`), restrict `seed_cycles` to {planner, implementer, tester, reviewer}. In run 01M0TKB7H7DCWCR8TZY6SZPXD2 the guard object carried unused `start` and `evidence` noise keys, making the tracker-empty/loop guard harder for the planner to read. Complementary to closed fabro-45d0 (which introduced the counter); this narrows its shape. Expected effect: self-explanatory guard object, fewer misreads at loop-boundary decisions.","labels":["revision"]}
